1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,245
For eight lectures, you've drawn every floor your crew walked on.

2
00:00:05,045 --> 00:00:06,673
Today they board a ship,

3
00:00:07,123 --> 00:00:08,654
and you draw nothing.

4
00:00:09,554 --> 00:00:11,907
The game builds her deck from her own plan.

5
00:00:13,707 --> 00:00:15,386
Your job is what's on it.

6
00:00:16,286 --> 00:00:20,426
A prisoner, a gunner with the cell your beacon needs,

7
00:00:20,876 --> 00:00:23,618
and a strongbox that ends it three ways.

8
00:00:25,418 --> 00:00:30,333
It's brand new, so at the end I'll show you what to check before your crew finds it.

9
00:00:31,533 --> 00:00:33,051
The button needs four things.

10
00:00:33,951 --> 00:00:35,486
A ship that has struck.

11
00:00:35,936 --> 00:00:37,303
A hull with a plan.

12
00:00:37,753 --> 00:00:40,689
The station art, which your starter already has.

13
00:00:42,489 --> 00:00:43,805
And no other party out.

14
00:00:44,705 --> 00:00:46,920
That last one is the trouble.

15
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:51,280
Your relay party opens in the first second,

16
00:00:51,730 --> 00:00:55,174
and a party on a map never closes by itself.

17
00:00:56,074 --> 00:00:57,823
So as your mission stands,

18
00:00:58,273 --> 00:01:00,438
with anybody still down at the relay,

19
00:01:00,888 --> 00:01:02,654
Comms can't send a party to her.

20
00:01:04,454 --> 00:01:06,052
We fix that with one rule.

21
00:01:06,502 --> 00:01:09,295
When she strikes, the landing party comes home.

22
00:01:10,195 --> 00:01:13,024
When the ship comes back, the relay opens again.

23
00:01:14,224 --> 00:01:16,414
Here she is on the Comms console,

24
00:01:16,864 --> 00:01:19,634
the Black Gull, a pirate, out past the relay.

25
00:01:20,534 --> 00:01:23,086
Hail, taunt, or tell her to surrender.

26
00:01:24,886 --> 00:01:27,399
In the file, first a side for her to be on.

27
00:01:27,849 --> 00:01:30,340
One record, and one line that says enemies.

28
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:34,116
Then the ship, in the story file.

29
00:01:34,566 --> 00:01:37,191
Two lines, under the relay's own line.

30
00:01:38,991 --> 00:01:41,805
Her hull is a pirate raider, with no fighter bay.

31
00:01:42,705 --> 00:01:44,335
A carrier brings its fighters,

32
00:01:44,785 --> 00:01:47,338
and they'd shoot at your ship all game.

33
00:01:49,138 --> 00:01:50,446
Look at the numbers.

34
00:01:51,346 --> 00:01:53,381
The first set is where she comes from.

35
00:01:53,831 --> 00:01:55,855
The second is where she is.

36
00:01:57,655 --> 00:02:01,841
That matters, because a ship that strikes and isn't boarded runs for home,

37
00:02:02,291 --> 00:02:05,076
and when she gets there she's taken off the map.

38
00:02:05,976 --> 00:02:07,561
I tried it with one place.

39
00:02:08,011 --> 00:02:11,108
She struck, and eight seconds later she was gone.

40
00:02:12,308 --> 00:02:14,452
Here's the chase in the Quest Log aboard,

41
00:02:14,902 --> 00:02:16,427
with her picture at the top.

42
00:02:18,227 --> 00:02:20,324
In the file there are three quests.

43
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:24,071
Run her down, which waits for the ship to close on her.

44
00:02:24,971 --> 00:02:27,783
Come back to the relay, which is hidden until then.

45
00:02:28,683 --> 00:02:32,726
And take her, which waits for a signal the game sends.

46
00:02:34,526 --> 00:02:36,297
Two of them get a page for the bridge.

47
00:02:36,747 --> 00:02:38,545
Her picture at the top of the chase,

48
00:02:38,995 --> 00:02:41,592
and two icon bullets on the prize.

49
00:02:43,392 --> 00:02:44,743
The card is one you know.

50
00:02:45,193 --> 00:02:47,429
It's the tug card from the first class,

51
00:02:47,879 --> 00:02:49,604
hearing a different step start.

52
00:02:51,404 --> 00:02:52,610
It does two things.

53
00:02:53,060 --> 00:02:56,249
It calls the landing party home, and she strikes.

54
00:02:58,049 --> 00:03:00,186
And the same line goes on your old card,

55
00:03:00,636 --> 00:03:01,841
for the trip back.

56
00:03:03,041 --> 00:03:06,823
Here's her deck, and the captain's strongbox, in her brig.

57
00:03:08,623 --> 00:03:11,754
In the file, two new words put it there.

58
00:03:12,654 --> 00:03:15,433
Area, deck: that means whatever ship we board.

59
00:03:17,233 --> 00:03:19,575
And mark is no longer a mark in a file,

60
00:03:20,025 --> 00:03:21,336
because there is no file.

61
00:03:22,236 --> 00:03:22,986
It's a kind of room.

62
00:03:23,436 --> 00:03:26,071
Brig, cargo, quarters, bay.

63
00:03:27,871 --> 00:03:30,060
Her hold is called the plunder hold.

64
00:03:30,510 --> 00:03:32,264
Her sickbay is the surgery.

65
00:03:33,164 --> 00:03:34,341
You don't need to know that.

66
00:03:34,791 --> 00:03:37,763
You write the kind, and it works on any hull.

67
00:03:39,562 --> 00:03:42,040
And when a hull has no such room,

68
00:03:42,490 --> 00:03:46,364
your thing stands in the hallway, and the game says so once.

69
00:03:47,564 --> 00:03:48,728
Here's her deck again.

70
00:03:49,628 --> 00:03:52,256
A few of her own crew stand about on it too,

71
00:03:52,706 --> 00:03:54,471
calm, and they won't fight.

72
00:03:56,271 --> 00:03:58,609
A calm person blocks the cell they stand on,

73
00:03:59,059 --> 00:04:00,707
and so does a strongbox.

74
00:04:01,607 --> 00:04:05,238
So the game walks the deck before it puts anything down.

75
00:04:06,138 --> 00:04:08,188
Nothing of yours stands in a doorway,

76
00:04:08,638 --> 00:04:10,580
or anywhere that would shut something in.

77
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:15,623
Where a thing stands can change when you add a record.

78
00:04:16,073 --> 00:04:18,983
What it can never do is block the way.

79
00:04:20,783 --> 00:04:24,442
So keep one rule: after every change to what's aboard,

80
00:04:24,892 --> 00:04:27,313
go aboard and walk to each thing.

81
00:04:28,513 --> 00:04:29,818
Now play it through.

82
00:04:30,718 --> 00:04:34,256
Helm closes to fifteen hundred, and she strikes.

83
00:04:35,156 --> 00:04:37,282
Comms selects her, and sends a party.

84
00:04:39,082 --> 00:04:41,962
Aboard, the gunner stands in the boat bay.

85
00:04:42,862 --> 00:04:44,139
Once the ship has struck,

86
00:04:44,589 --> 00:04:45,804
her crew stand down,

87
00:04:46,254 --> 00:04:47,415
and the gunner with them.

88
00:04:49,215 --> 00:04:51,250
She still carries the relay's cell.

89
00:04:52,150 --> 00:04:54,396
Walk up to her and ask for it,

90
00:04:54,846 --> 00:04:57,334
and she hands it over, no shot fired.

91
00:04:59,134 --> 00:05:01,984
The strongbox has three answers that matter.

92
00:05:02,884 --> 00:05:04,742
Take her, and she joins your side,

93
00:05:05,192 --> 00:05:06,323
and the quest pays.

94
00:05:07,223 --> 00:05:08,926
Scuttle her, and she's gone.

95
00:05:09,826 --> 00:05:12,073
Leave her, and she runs for home.

96
00:05:13,873 --> 00:05:16,098
Every one of them brings the party home first.

97
00:05:16,998 --> 00:05:18,328
And after every one,

98
00:05:18,778 --> 00:05:21,343
the relay opens again when the ship comes back.

99
00:05:22,543 --> 00:05:25,024
Lint says clean on your finished mission.

100
00:05:25,924 --> 00:05:28,398
What's left to know isn't in your file.

101
00:05:30,198 --> 00:05:32,316
A shot never removes a prop.

102
00:05:33,216 --> 00:05:35,700
The strongbox is safe from a full shot,

103
00:05:36,150 --> 00:05:38,552
and so is anything else that holds an ending.

104
00:05:40,352 --> 00:05:43,203
Comms has its own button, take as prize.

105
00:05:43,653 --> 00:05:46,461
It finishes the same quest as your strongbox,

106
00:05:46,911 --> 00:05:49,579
but nobody goes aboard to meet what you wrote.

107
00:05:51,379 --> 00:05:55,894
Somebody calm can't be shot, so the gunner's cell comes only from her answer.

108
00:05:57,694 --> 00:06:01,183
And from her deck, the transporter still reaches your relay.

109
00:06:02,083 --> 00:06:05,156
Know these before your crew finds them.

110
00:06:06,356 --> 00:06:07,359
Now it's your turn.

111
00:06:08,259 --> 00:06:09,775
Play all three endings.

112
00:06:10,675 --> 00:06:13,606
Move the strongbox into the cabin, and walk to it.

113
00:06:14,506 --> 00:06:17,993
Swap her hull for a freighter, and see where everything goes.

114
00:06:19,793 --> 00:06:22,241
Then light the beacon with the gunner's cell.

115
00:06:23,141 --> 00:06:25,070
Next time, the mission is your own.
